<section id="tableaux">
		<section>
			<h2>Tables</h2> 
			<p>Tables should be understandable when read linearly and not be too complex</p>
		</section>
			
		<section>
			<h2>Table Reading order</h2> 
			<ul>
				<li>Row by row, from left to right</li>
				<li>Each piece of data in separate cell</li>
				<li>
					<a target="tweede" href="http://examples.anysurfer.be/2.4.1/Linearisation_tableau_nok.htm">Bad example</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a target="tweede" href="http://examples.anysurfer.be/2.4.1/Linearisation_tableau_ok.htm">Good example</a>
				</li>
			
			</ul>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>Table structure</h2>
			<p>Tables are structured properly: <code is:raw>th</code> for headings, <code is:raw>caption</code> if needed</p> 
			<img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/structure/tableau_primes_modif_en.png" alt="table where caption and table headers are highlighted" />
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>Complex tables</h2> 
			<ul>
				<li>To be avoided</li>
				<li>Replace with several simple tables</li>
				<li>Use <code is:raw>headers</code> and <code is:raw>id</code> attributes if you cannot avoir complexity (<a href="http://examples.anysurfer.be/2.4.4/Tableau_complexe.php">example</a>)</li>
				<li><a href="http://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/tables/">Complex table tutorial</a></li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</section>
